// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Markus Neis
// Date: 2018-06-07 | Modified: 2023-02-07
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.005
// Description: Detects potential LethalHTA technique where the "mshta.exe" is spawned by an "svchost.exe"
//   process
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://codewhitesec.blogspot.com/2018/07/lethalhta.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_mshta_lethalhta_technique.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\svchost.exe" and FolderPath endswith "\\mshta.exe"
